{% doc %}
  Format Price

  Outputs a price in the design's display format (₹ prefix, comma thousands
  separator, `.00` dropped — e.g. ₹2,000; a real fractional price keeps its
  paise, e.g. ₹7,410.59). The single source for product-facing
  prices: price-row renders it into the page, and variant-selector renders it
  into its variant JSON so a client-side variant change shows the exact same
  string. Cart surfaces keep the store's own money format.

  @param {number} cents - Price in cents

  @example
  {% render 'format-price', cents: product.price %}
{% enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign formatted_amount = cents | default: 0 | money_without_currency | remove: '.00'
  echo '₹' | append: formatted_amount
-%}
